CORE
main.ii
--winx64 --cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ same type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ different types: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ hash of the same type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
With the MSVC runtime, typeid was rejected ("typeid requires <typeinfo>"):
type_info is declared in the global namespace.  Its comparison calls the
runtime's __std_type_info_compare, now modelled: cbmc gives each type one
type_info object, so they compare equal iff they are the same object.
